flowchart TD
    HW["<b>1. NIC + NAPI batch</b><br/>DMA fills RX descriptors, IRQ schedules NAPI<br/><b>handoff:</b> poll budget moves work out of hard IRQ<br/><b>state:</b> driver owns packet buffers"]

    XDP["<b>2. driver poll + native XDP</b><br/>driver reaps descriptors and runs XDP before skb allocation<br/><b>handoff:</b> only XDP_PASS enters the normal stack<br/><b>state:</b> packet may be dropped, redirected, TX'd, or passed"]

    SKB["<b>3. skb + protocol setup</b><br/>build_skb/napi_build_skb, eth_type_trans, optional GRO<br/><b>handoff:</b> generic stack needs skb metadata and protocol key<br/><b>state:</b> skb has L2/L3 offsets, protocol, and possible GRO aggregate"]

    CORE["<b>4. RX core policy</b><br/>taps, VLAN handling, tc ingress, packet_type dispatch<br/><b>handoff:</b> IPv4/IPv6 handler owns L3 parsing<br/><b>state:</b> skb is stack-owned and handler-selected"]

    IP["<b>5. IP + Netfilter</b><br/>header validation, PREROUTING, route lookup<br/><b>handoff:</b> ACCEPT plus dst decides local delivery or forwarding<br/><b>state:</b> skb may be rewritten, dropped, queued, or routed"]

    OUT["<b>6. local or forward path</b><br/>transport socket lookup or forwarding output path<br/><b>handoff:</b> L4 owns local payload, TX path owns transit skb<br/><b>state:</b> bytes reach TCP/UDP or leave RX path"]

    DONE["<b>XDP non-PASS</b><br/>normal skb path stops"]

    HW --> XDP --> SKB --> CORE --> IP --> OUT
    XDP -. DROP / TX / REDIRECT .-> DONE

    classDef hw fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    classDef napi fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:2px
    classDef stack fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px
    classDef ip fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef exit fill:#f3f4f6,stroke:#6b7280,stroke-width:2px
    class HW hw
    class XDP,SKB napi
    class CORE stack
    class IP,OUT ip
    class DONE exit
